The One Light and One Dark palettes are adapted from GitHub's Atom One themes
(styles/colors.less, styles/syntax-variables.less, styles/ui-variables.less):

- https://github.com/atom/one-light-syntax (revision d84579027410c576086dfca14d934c4bd74b0438)
- https://github.com/atom/one-dark-syntax (revision 9c96f4454362267ac45322063e193ccf9d2debb1)
- https://github.com/atom/one-light-ui (revision a27bce35088ecd323e44f5c2510bcf2d4e9efcf8)
- https://github.com/atom/one-dark-ui (revision 18c2143d41e17b337fff6dc7024562c4d999be17)

The exact HSL definitions are kept. Atom defines no terminal palette, so the
ANSI slots reuse One's syntax hues. Adapted to OpenIDEA's design tokens by bghtyu.

